   "reason": "Maintainer fixes after the first review (2026-11-19; the maintainers' decision: keep tests/hidden/episodes.json and tests/units.json byte-identical, so the 12 episodes, their units, seeds, counters, refill lists and trays stay what they were). Frozen files that changed, and what each change does to an episode: (1) tests/episode.py and solution/oracle/episode.py (byte-identical): the credit follows the job: a listed jar is done when it holds exactly the listed pieces of its kind and nothing else and is closed again (opened in the episode, its own lid seated, closing torque 0.5-2.5 N m); the episode's credit is the done jars over the listed jars; the unlisted jar is judged by how it ends (halved if something was put into it or it was opened and not closed again properly); the other halvings and the end of an episode are unchanged. The reference does the whole job, so its credit stays 1.0 on every episode. (2) tests/jar_sim.py and solution/oracle/jar_sim.py (byte-identical): one renderer per image size, kept for the episode's model, instead of one per image (20 images compared with the old path: byte-identical, the noise drawn exactly as before); the robots' collision geoms move to a geom group no camera shows (a rendering label: contacts unchanged); joint angles in an action are clipped to the joints' limits and a non-finite control ends the episode as unstable (the reference sends 7-number Cartesian steps only). (3) tests/jar_env.py and solution/oracle/jar_env.py (byte-identical): the renderer cache; the probe's perturbed copy keeps the observed hand and wrist-camera poses' relation to the joints (the same offsets, drawn in the same order); the real observation is unchanged. (4) tests/jar_grade.py: the 9000 s budget is charged to the controller's own time (READY and every reply, plus image_cost_s per image asked for) instead of the wall clock with the grader's simulation and rendering in it; the wire, the probe lock and its schedule are unchanged. (5) tests/grader_config.json: image_cost_s 0.2 added. (6) solution/oracle/wire_world.py: the oracle waits for the reference's action instead of answering a hold after 20 s of wall time. Not in the frozen list and changed in the same commit: tests/verify.py (the kit's clear_agent_account called first and its report read; the numerics fingerprint checked before grading; the controller clock), tests/numerics_check.py and tests/numerics.json (new), environment/Dockerfile (OPENBLAS_CORETYPE=Haswell and OPENBLAS_L2_SIZE=256, WORKDIR /). The pinned kernel changes the simulation's last bits on hosts that used another kernel (the selection's host was one): with it the reference takes other numbers of steps on the 12 episodes than in the selection's runs, the same numbers on every host, and completes every one of them (the evidence). None of the code changes moves the reference by a bit: on a host whose own kernel is the pinned one, the 12 episodes take exactly the steps they took before the changes.",
